{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And you, here, etc.</b> The meaning is: since Israel had not made Moses an agent to receive HaShem's commandments until now, therefore HaShem decided on their behalf and appointed him as agent and said to him, <b>״And you, here,״ etc., ״and I will speak to you all the commandment,״</b> etc. Or perhaps the intent is to say that when the commandment reaches Moses from HaShem it is as though it has already been received by Israel, for they have made him their agent — just as a woman's agent to receive her kiddushin, such that once the agent has received them it is as though they have reached the woman's hand, for his hand is like her hand. So too when Moses receives the commandment it is as though Israel have received it. And this is what it says, <b>״and I will speak to you,״</b> and when the matter reaches you, you shall make it known to them and they shall perform it — and this is what it says, ״you shall teach them and they shall perform.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:31.998016702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}